<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16453" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵσταμαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>never standing still, unresting,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κύκλῳ σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					1073a31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τροχός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mesom.
					<u>Nem.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, φορεῖθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.181
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				27.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>unsteady, unstable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					3p.65U.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.166S.
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.230
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Diog.Oen.
				18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diogenian.Epicur.
				2.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.103f
			</span></i>; of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. τὴν διάνοιαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Onos.
					3.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. αἰών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					7.2543
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θνητῶν βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					699
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.651
			</span></i>; of a house, <i>ruinous, PLond.ined.</i><i><span class="en">
				2194
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>uncertain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					6.57.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>making it impossible to stand,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνος, πάθος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Ocyp.</u>
				36
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				71
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>unweighed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				1.32<i>B</i>25
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				602
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
